WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.950
You asked your agent for one small change.

2
00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:08.470
It edited five files, missed the sixth, and told you it was [bleep] done.

3
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.470
It called a flag that doesn't exist. Three times.

4
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.430
Then it wrote your release notes like a [bleep] sales pitch.

5
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:21.530
Your agent isn't [bleep]. Your code and your docs are making it guess.

6
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.150
And the same things trip up your users.

7
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:29.250
Agent ergonomics. One free skill, for any coding agent.

8
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.550
Install it with one command.

9
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.600
Then ask in plain words.

10
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:39.460
It finds the code that should live together, writes the plan, and measures before and after.

11
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:42.740
It strips the hype and the filler out of your words.

12
00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.600
And it cuts the jargon a new user meets.

13
00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:50.150
So your agents stop guessing. And so do your users.

14
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.150
agentergonomics.org

